id: blueprint
name: Blueprint
kind: gear
# Gained through the Create Maneuver, never given or crafted: no Craft DC.
special: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  What something made through the Create Maneuver is recorded on: making it again with Create succeeds
  without the Check.
text: >
  Blueprint: Once you have created anything through the Create Maneuver, you gain a Blueprint of what was
  created. A Blueprint is a Basic Item that can be used when using the Create Maneuver to instantly
  succeed at recreating whatever is recorded on the Blueprint.

---

# Given by Create's Made it - named "Blueprint: <what>", and what it records kept on it (a Basic Item's
# file, or a Weapon's, Apparel's, Vehicle's or Battle Jacket's name, asked). One for each thing: a second
# of the same is not given. Picked in Create's list, it skips the Check alone (the user's ruling): the
# Scrap or Ingredient, the Time Cost and the Session Limit are paid as ever, and the card says it
# succeeds. A Blueprint's making is not recorded on another.
